ff61c7461f6df995865a6be6a00d60a3245", "bytes": 201583, "lines": 469, "events_no_deltas": [{"type": "system", "subtype": "init", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "tools": ["StructuredOutput"], "mcp_servers": [], "permissionMode": "auto", "claude_code_version": "2.1.294", "output_style": "default", "init_sha256": "19a6ffcf0781096cd8fadcc901d1f698c81748761870f4f438dc6f07a56b3d9a"}, {"type": "system", "subtype": "status", "status": "requesting"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "message_start", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgQXe1eQCucW9EU7pWG5L", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3841, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3841}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "ttft_ms": 2084, "thinking_display": "updates"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 0, "content_block": {"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "thinking_display": "updates"}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgQXe1eQCucW9EU7pWG5L", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": {"длина": 38096, "sha256": "68c98b31fc4ceb08a557f829fe534665b35cf8f10b57930fc54795f40c4df8d8"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3841, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3841}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T08:27:41.265Z", "request_id": "req_011CgQXe1LYTzjFZJmGfn2yE", "thinking_duration_ms": 139622}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 0}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 1, "content_block": {"type": "text", "text": ""}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgQXe1eQCucW9EU7pWG5L", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I pick **Candidate 6**. Candidate 0 is a close second, and every other plan is clearly worse. All figures below are rough estimates I worked out by hand.\n\n**How I compared them.** Each plan orders a fixed multiple k of the forecast for the day the order arrives. Plan 3 is the exception: it orders every other day, two days' worth at a time.\n\n| Candidate | k for item 0 | k for item 1 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 1.05 | 1.05 |\n| 1 | 1.00 | 1.15 |\n| 2 | 0.90 | 0.90 |\n| 3 (every 2 days) | 1.075 | 1.08 |\n| 4 | 1.15 | 1.00 |\n| 5 | 1.11 | 1.095 |\n| 6 | 1.00 | 1.00 |\n| 7 | 1.25 | 1.25 |\n\n**What every plan loses the same way.** Item 0's first delivery only arrives on day 5. The starting stock of 39 can't cover days 0–4, so all plans pay the same shortage penalties there. Cash never runs short, even for plan 7 at its lowest point (about 880 on day 5). The 220-unit warehouse limit only becomes a risk for plans 3 and 7.\n\n**Why ordering more than the forecast doesn't pay.** The orders are fixed in advance. Leftovers carry over to later days (they last 4–5 days), so stock behaves like a random walk that drifts upward when k is above mean demand (about 1.046 × forecast):\n- Item 0: going from k = 1.05 to 1.11 saves about 20 units of shortage (about 255). But it costs about 264 more in purchases and about 210 more in storage. Net loss is about 230; at k = 1.15 the loss is about 460.\n- Item 1: the purchase price of 11 is high next to the sale price of 15. At k = 1.15 the extra purchases (about 1,185) and storage (about 350) far outweigh the 608 saved on shortages. Net loss is about 930; at k = 1.095 it is about 280.\n- Unsold stock is wasted at the end, and an over-ordering plan carries a larger leftover.\n- Ordering too little also loses. At k = 0.9, shortages cost about 160 extra on item 0 and about 340 extra on item 1 compared with k = 1.0.\n- Plan 3 saves 14 order fees (about 392). But it holds an extra day's demand every second night, about 38 per cycle or 530 in total. Add its k of about 1.08, and it ends up about 400 worse.\n\n**Overall** (loss compared with ordering exactly mean demand, about 1.046 × forecast; lower is better):\n\n| Candidate | Estimated loss |\n|---|---|\n| 6 | about −140 (best) |\n| 0 | about +20 |\n| 4 | about +350 |\n| 2 | about +385 |\n| 3 | about +410 |\n| 5 | about +500 |\n| 1 | about +900 |\n| 7 | much worse |\n\nRandom demand doesn't change the order. Plans with a higher k have larger, more variable leftovers and waste more at the end. Plan 6 keeps stock small and stays far from the warehouse limit. The 160 gap between plans 6 and 0 is small compared with how rough these numbers are, but the model favours plan 6 on both items."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3841, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3841}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T08:27:52.364Z", "request_id": "req_011CgQXe1LYTzjFZJmGfn2yE"}, {"type": "stream_event", 